-- title:
--   Maximality of primes over the supersingular point on blow-up charts
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and assume $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ equal (`hH₁`) to the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ coming from $\ell \mid q^2M'$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{Laurent}(L)$ equal (`hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of level [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133).
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, an $L$-algebra which is a fraction ring of $A$ (so $L$ is its fraction field), such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $j$-expansion read in $L$ (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A ↥K j` for $j$ viewed in $C$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), supersingular in the sense (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Throughout, $\Gamma_0(M')$, $\Gamma(q)$ are the usual congruence subgroups of $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and for $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and $\tau$ an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$, the predicate [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) says that $\tau$ realises the action of $\gamma^{-1}$ on $q$-expansions at level [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133): for every weight $k$, every pair $f, g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for that level with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $g$ having nonzero expansion, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is that of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i /q}$, the $\iota$-image of the expansion of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   **The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis asserts, for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two chart spectra over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$) such that the germ at $z$ of the pullback of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$ above, the existence of: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f u\big)$, subject to seven clauses: (i) $e$ carries the image of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are $\theta \in \mathrm{Aut}(S)$, $c \in W$ and $M \in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $e$ with the action of $\tau$ on germs at $z$ of elements of $C$, $\theta$ fixes the classes of constants, $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1 \bmod \ell$ forces $c \equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak{m}_W$, and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity then $c \not\equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak{m}_W$; (v) two primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each omitting one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and containing respectively $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ up to an element of $(X_0,X_1)^2$, have distinct contractions to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along $e$ whenever $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (v) containing $X_0$ up to $(X_0,X_1)^2$, and $a \in C$, the germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with $\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0 \in y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a, b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e$ sends the germ of $\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0$ to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The chosen point and presentation.** Fix a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the pullback of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ with `ιFin` image $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (`hy'y`). Fix data $W_1, \sigma_1, \mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units, $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\big)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for these data exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) above.
--
--   **The ideal $J$ and the algebras.** Let $J \subset C$ be (`hJ`) the infimum of the ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism for $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, take the pullback along the induced endomorphism of $C$ of the contraction, along $e_1$ composed with completion and the germ map at $z$, of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $B \subset K$ be the $A$-subalgebra (`hB`) generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x\,\varpi_t = i\}$, i.e. $C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   Four further hypothesis blocks are imposed. `hR1`: $C \le B$, and every $f \in K$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$. `hR2`: $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $W$ and in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $f \in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses): first, for every $(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k_A`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k_A[X_0,X_1]$ by the Drinfeld relation) whose kernel is $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, which on $A$ is the residue map followed by the structure map, and which is equivariant for level automorphisms: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism for $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, there are $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) such that $\rho \circ \tau =$ `hAction` of that element applied to $\rho$, and $c \neq 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; second, $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; third, every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ admits $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ for $\gamma^{-1}$ carrying every element of $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ into $Q$; fourth, an element $b \in B$ all of whose images under such $\tau$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by the image of $\varpi$; fifth, a level automorphism $\tau$ for $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, that preserves $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $a \in C$ with $a \in J$ and $a \neq 0$ in $K$, put
--   $$B_a := C\big[\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x\,a = i\}\big] \subset K,$$
--   the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by the quotients of $J$ by $a$. Then every prime ideal $Q$ of $B_a$ such that
--
--   1. for every $c \in C$ whose image in $K$ lies in $B_a$, $c \in y$ implies that the corresponding element of $B_a$ lies in $Q$, and
--
--   2. whenever $\varpi_t\,a^{-1} \in B_a$, that element lies in $Q$,
--
--   is a maximal ideal of $B_a$.
--
--   This is the local step showing that, on each affine blow-up chart $C[J/a]$ of the supersingular chart of the integral model, a prime lying over the supersingular point $y$ and containing $\varpi_t/a$ is closed: it identifies the $T=0$ locus of the exceptional fibre with a point. It is the variant of this step for the auxiliary level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with the $\ell$-diamond condition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ in place of a full auxiliary level, and it feeds the assembly statement on the primes over a supersingular point lying on a unique component.
